      "content": "That feeling of being an empty room is incredibly lonely, and it suggests you are deeply tired of the fight. If the person who was supposed to watch is gone, then the next step might be to let the room be quiet, but not necessarily empty. Sometimes, allowing the pressure to ease—even just a little—is the only way to find a different kind of peace. Please consider contacting a mental health professional; they can help you explore what that true, restful stillness might look like without the finality you fear.",
